      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "The Recursion Trap",
          "text": "A method that borrows and then calls itself borrows twice and panics. Restructure so the guard is passed down instead."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Misread Clones"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`a.clone()` on `Rc<Vec<T>>` clones the pointer",
            "Not the vector — obvious to Rust, surprising in review",
            "`==` on two `Rc`s compares the pointed-to values",
            "`Rc::ptr_eq` is the identity test"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "drop() And get_mut()",
          "items": [
            "`drop(x)` on an `Rc` merely decrements",
            "It frees early only when no clone exists",
            "`Rc::get_mut` returning `None` means still shared",
            "That is a signal, not a bug"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Design Smells"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`Rc<RefCell<T>>` where `&mut` plus a restructure would do",
            "It trades compile errors for runtime panics",
